# Dual jump: first taken -> 0x40, else second taken -> 0x80. Both test bit 0 of the same P0,
# so exactly one is always taken and the fallthrough to the packet end is infeasible.
# The constant domain can't relate the two conditions with P0 unknown, so absint also follows
# the infeasible fallthrough and adds the jumpr R31 after the packet as a block. RzAnalysisBlock
# only has jump/fail, so that third edge is dropped and the block has no incoming edge.
# A precise analysis would produce only the 0x40 and 0x80 edges and no block after the packet.
